{
  "_comment": [
    "SeSystemtimePrivilege for timed, and for nothing else.",
    "",
    "authd unions the privileges of every SID on a token, and a service",
    "token carries the S-1-5-80 service SID derived from the service name.",
    "So a record named for that SID grants the privilege to this one",
    "service -- not to LocalService, which trustd and resolvd also are.",
    "",
    "The SID below is SHA-1 of 'TIMED' as upper-cased UTF-16LE, read as five",
    "little-endian u32s, which is the derivation authd and peinit both",
    "implement (authd/src/service_sid.rs). It is written out rather than",
    "computed because a .reg file cannot compute; if the service is ever",
    "renamed this value must be recomputed, and timed will lose the",
    "privilege silently if it is not -- the symptom is adjtimex failing",
    "with EPERM and the clock never being steered.",
    "",
    "This is separate from timed-service.reg on purpose. A privilege grant",
    "is a different kind of statement from a service definition, an image",
    "may reasonably want to review or withhold it, and an administrator",
    "looking for 'what on this machine may set the clock' should find one",
    "file that answers it.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the timed package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy\\S-1-5-80-2061758774-2413367500-3090050229-3167896262-4120155161",
      "values": [
        {
          "name": "Privileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["SeSystemtimePrivilege", "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
